You are implementing the changes required for Linear ticket {{ inputs.linear_id }}.

## Step 1 — Fetch the ticket

Run this exact command to get the ticket details. Do not use Notion, the Linear
web app, or any MCP tool — use the API directly:

```bash
curl -s -X POST https://api.linear.app/graphql \
  -H "Authorization: $LINEAR_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"query":"query{issue(id:\"{{ inputs.linear_id }}\"){identifier title description state{name} labels{nodes{name}} url}}"}'
```

Read the `title`, `description`, and acceptance criteria from the output.

## Step 2 — Implement

Follow `skills/test-driven-development.md`:
- Write failing tests first, then make them pass.
- Keep the diff focused — no drive-by refactors or unrelated cleanup.
- Write or update tests for every changed behaviour; run them and confirm they pass.

## Step 3 — Verify

Run the full verification gate before submitting:

```bash
uv run ruff check .
uv run mypy harness
uv run pytest
```

All three must be clean.

## Step 4 — Submit

When the work is complete and verified, call {{ submit_tool_name | default('submit') }} exactly once with no arguments — the file mutations are the output.
